Validatopia Wallet (Android) includes the following third-party libraries for reading
passport chips. They are used unmodified, as separate libraries fetched from Maven Central
at build time, and can be replaced with modified versions by changing the versions in
gradle/libs.versions.toml and rebuilding.

JMRTD 0.8.8 (org.jmrtd:jmrtd), https://jmrtd.org/
  GNU Lesser General Public License (LGPL), https://www.gnu.org/licenses/lgpl.html
  Source: https://repo1.maven.org/maven2/org/jmrtd/jmrtd/0.8.8/

SCUBA (net.sf.scuba:scuba-smartcards 0.0.21, net.sf.scuba:scuba-sc-android 0.0.27),
http://scuba.sourceforge.net/
  GNU Lesser General Public License (LGPL), https://www.gnu.org/licenses/lgpl.html
  Source: https://repo1.maven.org/maven2/net/sf/scuba/

EJBCA CVC 1.4.13 (org.ejbca.cvc:cert-cvc), a JMRTD dependency
  GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2.1,
  https://www.gnu.org/licenses/old-licenses/lgpl-2.1.html
  Source: https://repo1.maven.org/maven2/org/ejbca/cvc/cert-cvc/1.4.13/

It also includes:

Bouncy Castle (org.bouncycastle:bcprov-jdk18on and related), under the Bouncy Castle
licence: https://www.bouncycastle.org/licence.html

Google ML Kit text recognition and face detection, under the ML Kit Terms of Service:
https://developers.google.com/ml-kit/terms
